
======================================================================================================================
PART 0. THE APPARATUS: one law on the step B of a world line
======================================================================================================================
ok   the law: det(I - uB) = (1 - u^2)^24 k0 k2^10 k4^5, k_N(u) = 1 + 4u^2 - u(5 - 2N); one leading zero, k0(1/4) = 0
ok   the comparison is the propagation kernel: T = H W^T is unitary, T^dagger (6I - L) T = 5I - A, and det(I - uB) = (1 - u^2)^24 u^16 det[(6I - L) + chi(u) I], chi(u) = (1 - u)(1 - 4u)/u
ok   the grade factors are the spectral parameter read through the comparison: k_N(u) = u(2N + chi(u)), 6 - L = 0, 4, 8 at N = 0, 2, 4; the four points put the spectral parameter at chi = 0, -5 - 3i, -10, -5 + 3i; L(Omega) = 6
    the spectral parameter at the four points: singlet 1/4 -> chi = 0 (the one zero); direction h i/4 -> -5 - 3i; plane hk -1/4 -> -10; colour -i/4 -> -5 + 3i
    at u = -1/4 the comparison shifted by chi = -10 has the values -10, -6, -2 on the singlet, the symmetric states and the vector states:
    k_N(-1/4) = 5/2, 3/2, 1/2; transmission t = 1/k0 = 2/5, reflection e = k2/k0 = 3/5, at a single direction t_l = 1/k2 = 2/3, e_l = k4/k2 = 1/3
ok   one step out and back: F(z) = z^4(1 + z)/(16 - 8z - 3z^2 - 3z^3), signed Phi(z) = -z^4/(16 + 3z^2), counted on B
ok   one excursion: visits E n_F = 10, E n_L = 5, Var n_F = 84, Var n_L = 12, Cov = 30; 74 directed edges, M = 296 available transitions, C_h = 60 along h; b = 7/16
ok   a transition compares the moment with itself: <Omega, (L + g_h x g_s) Omega> = 6 + [s = h], computed from the comparison   [7, 6, 6, 6, 6]
ok   the cells: 16 vertices, 40 links, 40 squares; the curvature around the squares vanishes on every gauge transformation, C grad = 0
ok   the primitive numbers: grade factors 5/2, 3/2, 1/2; Phi(1) = -1/19, Phi(i) = -1/13; a = 5/38, chi_A = 13/12, eta = 295/296, c_L = 15/74, E_H = 3, f = 9/250, W = (2/5)^48 (295/296)^9
ok   the chart carries the same law: on a 3^4 chart (162 vertices, 405 links) det(I - uB_chart) = (1 - u^2)^(E - V) det((1 + 4u^2) - uA_chart)

======================================================================================================================
PART 1. THE LAW ANSWERS THE CLASSICAL CONTROLS: hold one quantity, vary it, watch what stays fixed
======================================================================================================================

F1. THE PLANE HK HELD, TYPE 2|4. Control: the null directions of the distinction. Answer: the null cone, projectivized, has three
    directions of one sign and one of the other. Form: one time and three space, the light cone.
ok   F1 the null cone of the distinction of the plane hk has signature (1, 3), negative directions first: one time, three space
    the clocks: rotations within the sides of d|6-d = [15, 10, 7, 6]; a central one only at 2|4. Own clock i g_h on the plane {n, h}; common clock
    g_h g_k on the plane hk; H_k (i g_h) H_k^dagger = g_h g_k; with i g_k they are one quaternion triple. Time is a held plane.
ok   F1 the two clocks are one quaternion triple: H_k (i g_h) H_k^dagger = g_h g_k, T_a^2 = -1, T1 T2 = T3, T2 T3 = T1, T3 T1 = T2; rotations within the sides 15, 10, 7, 6, central only at 2|4

F2. A WAVE OF A HELD WAVE VECTOR k. Control: k in all four directions of the chart, |k| varied. Answer: the law's operator Q(k).
    |k| = 0.4    (Q(k) - M^2)/|k|^2 over eight directions: 0.986222 to 0.988710
    |k| = 0.2    (Q(k) - M^2)/|k|^2 over eight directions: 0.996538 to 0.997167
    |k| = 0.1    (Q(k) - M^2)/|k|^2 over eight directions: 0.999133 to 0.999291
    |k| = 0.05   (Q(k) - M^2)/|k|^2 over eight directions: 0.999783 to 0.999823
    the step's weight held below the zero, u = 1/4 - m^2/24, m = 0.2, 0.1, 0.05: M^2/m^2 = 1.010985, 1.002728, 1.000681
    the spectral parameter there, chi/(m^2/2) = 1.008949, 1.002226, 1.000556: the mass squared is twice the spectral parameter to leading order; exactly M^2 = 2 chi + chi^2/5 on this chart
    a world line held at rest: its clock's frequency w where Q has its zero, w/M at M = 0.2, 0.1, 0.05: 0.997928, 0.999480, 0.999870
    Form: Q = M^2 + |k|^2 + O(|k|^4) in every direction, E^2 = p^2 c^2 + m^2 c^4 on the null cone of the plane hk; the zero's distance is the mass;
    at rest the clock turns at the mass, E = mc^2; c is one step per step.
ok   F2 Klein-Gordon: (Q - M^2)/|k|^2 -> 1 in every direction as k -> 0, M^2/m^2 -> 1, the rest frequency w/M -> 1

F3. A WORLD LINE CARRIED ALONG ANOTHER DIRECTION. Control: the clock's phase mu per step and the phase k along another direction, varied.
    Answer: U + U^dagger = 2 cos k cos mu at every (mu, k). Form: cos w = cos mu cos k, w^2 = mu^2 + k^2 at small phase: Dirac.
ok   F3 Dirac: the first-order step U = exp(-ik g_j) exp(-i mu g_h) has U + U^dagger = 2 cos k cos mu

F4. TWO SOURCES HELD AT REST AT A DISTANCE r. Control: r from 4 to 18 steps along four directions; the step's weight at the
    zero (M = 0) and below it (M = 0.05). Answer: the law's static response between the two held vertices, computed on the chart.
ok   F4 a static field on the chart lives on the projection of the A4 lattice along the direction h (cell 1/2); its operator is the chart's Q at k.T = 0
    direction [2, -1, 0]  M = 0: the number in front of 1/(4 pi r), from r = 6.54 to 17.44: 0.99891;   M = 0.05: 4 pi r G e^(Mr) at r = 4.4, 8.7, 13.1, 17.4: 0.9956, 1.0016, 1.0020, 1.0033; all 7 samples 0.99557 to 1.00331
    direction [1, 2, 3]   M = 0: the number in front of 1/(4 pi r), from r = 6.71 to 17.89: 0.99572;   M = 0.05: 4 pi r G e^(Mr) at r = 4.5, 8.9, 13.4, 17.9: 1.0050, 1.0002, 1.0014, 1.0030; all 7 samples 0.99913 to 1.00504
    direction [1, 1, 0]   M = 0: the number in front of 1/(4 pi r), from r = 6.00 to 18.00: 0.99304;   M = 0.05: 4 pi r G e^(Mr) at r = 4.0, 6.0, 8.0, 10.0: 0.9998, 0.9961, 0.9976, 0.9988; all 16 samples 0.99059 to 1.00280
    direction [1, 0, 0]   M = 0: the number in front of 1/(4 pi r), from r = 6.06 to 18.19: 0.99989;   M = 0.05: 4 pi r G e^(Mr) at r = 4.3, 6.1, 7.8, 9.5: 1.0061, 1.0027, 1.0024, 1.0021; all 17 samples 1.00077 to 1.00613
    Form: G_cont(r) = e^(-Mr)/(4 pi r), the long-wave continuum response: at the law's zero the response falls as 1/r (Poisson), below it as Yukawa with range 1/M;
    the step's weight for M = 0.05 is u = 0.249895904167. The number in front of 1/r is what the two held sources bring: PART 2.
ok   F4 the static response at the law's zero is 1/(4 pi r) within 1% in four directions; below the zero e^(-Mr)/(4 pi r) within 1% at r >= 4

F5. A GAUGE FIELD HELD ON THE LINKS. Control: phases theta on the forty links, amplitude varied; and a pure gauge transformation theta = grad phi.
    the plane hk and the singlet, w = 1/5 kappa from the answer at amplitudes 0.1, 0.03, 0.01: 0.004972, 0.004998, 0.005000   (2w^4/(1 - 5w^2)^2 = 0.005000)
    the direction h and colour, w = i/3 kappa from the answer at amplitudes 0.1, 0.03, 0.01: 0.010134, 0.010198, 0.010203   (2w^4/(1 - 5w^2)^2 = 0.010204)
    the spectral parameter varied, w = 1/(chi + 5): chi = 0, 1, 3, 10: kappa from the answer 0.0049997, 0.0020810, 0.0005745, 0.0000413; 2/[(chi + 5)^2 - 5]^2 = 0.0050000, 0.0020812, 0.0005745, 0.0000413
    a gauge transformation theta = grad phi at amplitude one changes the law by 2.2e-16
    Form: -(kappa/2)|C theta|^2, the squared curvature around the squares, unchanged by a gauge transformation: Maxwell's and Yang-Mills' F^2.
ok   F5 the law answers a gauge field with the squared curvature: kappa -> 1/200 and 1/98; as chi varies kappa(chi) = 2/[(chi + 5)^2 - 5]^2; a gauge transformation leaves it unchanged

F6. A CIRCULATION CARRIED AROUND THE CELLS. Control: the part of the link phases no gauge transformation removes, amplitude varied.
    Answer: the law's leading zero moves; |theta_cyc|^2/log 4u_c at amplitudes 0.03, 0.01, 0.003: 47.98761, 47.99862, 47.99988
    Form: log 4u_c = |theta_cyc|^2/48 + O(theta^4): the leading zero feels a rotation carried around the cells through 48 = k_C E l steps.
ok   F6 a circulation moves the leading zero by |theta_cyc|^2/48

F7. THE FRAME HELD CURVED. Control: the ten rotations split at h, the four that move it held as e/l, l varied; any curvature R.
    Answer: the curvature of the ten rotations contracted with h in the epsilon contraction, -(4/l^2)(R - 2 Lambda); Lambda l^2 at l = 0.5, 1, 1.7, 3: 3.000000000000, 3.000000000000, 3.000000000000, 3.000000000000
    Form: Einstein-Cartan with the constant term, R - 2 Lambda, Lambda = 3/l^2 for every curvature and every l.
ok   F7 Lambda l^2 = 3 at every l and every curvature

F8. THE DIRECTION h HELD AT ITS LENGTH v. Control: the direction h in the plane hk, length v varied; the twelve rotations keeping 2 + 3.
    v = 0.5  the moved rotations' masses squared over v^2: 0.500000, 0.500000, 0.800000; rotations left at zero: 9
    v = 1.0  the moved rotations' masses squared over v^2: 0.500000, 0.500000, 0.800000; rotations left at zero: 9
    v = 2.0  the moved rotations' masses squared over v^2: 0.500000, 0.500000, 0.800000; rotations left at zero: 9
    Form: |D(v h)|^2: W+, W-, Z with M^2 proportional to v^2, M_W^2/M_Z^2 = 5/8 at the source; the photon and eight colour rotations stay at zero.
ok   F8 the direction h at length v: masses squared v^2 (1/2, 1/2, 4/5), nine at zero, for every v

F9. A WORLD LINE HELD AT REST, ITS CLOCK TURNING. Control: a phase theta per step on its transitions, varied. Answer: the turn of the law's zero.
ok   F9 one transition marked, exactly: D_theta(u) = D(u) + (e^(-i theta) - 1) u D'(u)/320 at every u and theta (each transition one cofactor)
    theta = 0.0004  electron, one transition: turn per step x 320 = 0.999999975;   proton, each of its M transitions at L(Omega) = 6 and its C_h transitions along h once more: x 320 = 1836.000097;   ratio 1836.000144
    theta = 0.0002  electron, one transition: turn per step x 320 = 0.999999994;   proton, each of its M transitions at L(Omega) = 6 and its C_h transitions along h once more: x 320 = 1836.000024;   ratio 1836.000036
    theta = 0.0001  electron, one transition: turn per step x 320 = 0.999999998;   proton, each of its M transitions at L(Omega) = 6 and its C_h transitions along h once more: x 320 = 1836.000006;   ratio 1836.000009
    the ratio at theta -> 0: 1836.000000 = L(Omega) M + C_h = 6 x 296 + 60
    Form: a world line at rest turns its clock at a fixed rate per step, E = hbar w = mc^2; the electron's is one transition in 320, the unit; the
    proton's 1836 transitions' worth; the ratio of the two clocks is the ratio of the two masses.
ok   F9 the zero turns by theta/320 + O(theta^3) per marked transition, rate 1/320 as theta -> 0; the proton's rate on the available transitions is 6M + C_h = 1836 times the electron's as theta -> 0

F10. THE SPECTRAL PARAMETER VARIED: A RESPONSE AND ITS OWN CLOCK. Control: chi, from the zero (chi = 0) to the empty step (chi -> infinity).
    On the fifteen states other than the singlet the comparison's resolvent weighs a symmetric state by 1/(chi + 4) and a vector state by 1/(chi + 8).
    Answer: the covariance of the grade N with H_D H_E, H_D(S) = (5|S cap D| - |D||S|)/4, against the clock C_W = (9/8) Var N.
    chi = 0        response of a pair of directions on opposite sides 0.010000, its clock C_W 0.720000; ratios 0.01388889, 0.05555556, 0.08333333
    chi = 0.5      response of a pair of directions on opposite sides 0.010343, its clock C_W 0.744727; ratios 0.01388889, 0.05555556, 0.08333333
    chi = 2        response of a pair of directions on opposite sides 0.011095, its clock C_W 0.798817; ratios 0.01388889, 0.05555556, 0.08333333
    chi = 10       response of a pair of directions on opposite sides 0.012600, its clock C_W 0.907200; ratios 0.01388889, 0.05555556, 0.08333333
    chi = 1e+06    response of a pair of directions on opposite sides 0.013889, its clock C_W 0.999999; ratios 0.01388889, 0.05555556, 0.08333333
    Form: J_DE = (C_W/72)(|D||E| - 5 tr P_D P_E) at regular chi: the response and the clock move together and their ratio stays.
    What stays: 1/72 for one pair of directions on opposite sides, the strong and the electroweak coupling squared; 4/72 = 1/18 for one direction against the other
    four, which is -Phi(1)/(1 + Phi(1)) of the signed first return at the even points, counted on the walk; 6/72 = 1/12 for the plane hk against its
    three outside directions, -Phi(i)/(1 + Phi(i)) at the odd points. At the zero the response is 1/100 and the clock 18/25.
ok   F10 chi varied: response/clock = 1/72, 1/18, 1/12 at regular chi, equal to g^2, -Phi(1)/(1 + Phi(1)), -Phi(i)/(1 + Phi(i)); 1/100 and 18/25 at the zero

F11. THE NUCLEON PROJECTED. Control: the three colour world lines' spin and isospin, symmetric under exchange (the colour state is
    totally antisymmetric); the proton with spin up singled out. Answer: the axial current sum_r sigma_z tau_z in that state.
    the symmetric space has rank 20; P_N = P_sym(15/4 - S^2)/3 has rank 4; in the proton with spin up <sum sigma_z tau_z> = 1.666666666667
    Form: the axial coupling g_A = <p| sum sigma_z tau_z |p> times the transmission to the power 2b/3, (5/3) t^(2b/3).
ok   F11 the nucleon projected: rank 4 in the symmetric 20; <sum_r sigma_z tau_z> = 5/3 in the proton with spin up

======================================================================================================================
PART 2. THE EXPERIMENTS: the numerical catalogue under its stated controls
======================================================================================================================
Each experiment: what is held (the classical quantities, as the experimenter holds them); what the law returns at the breaking
that holding fixes; the classical form the answer has; and what remains when the answer is written in that form: the number.

A. GRAVITATION: the singlet, type 0|6, u = 1/4, the law's leading zero

EXPERIMENT A1. Newton: two protons held at rest at a distance r
  held:            two world lines at rest, each a proton, at distances r from 4 to 18 steps of the law's chart; they
                   meet at the singlet, which divides nothing.
  the law returns: the static response at the law's zero, 1/(4 pi r) (F4), times what the two sources bring to the
                   singlet: each source passes a whole excursion on each of its colour directions, k_C = 3 directions
                   of E l = 16 steps each at the transmission t = 1/k0(-1/4) = 2/5, and k_C E_H = 9 transitions along
                   h each reached at eta = 295/296: W = t^48 eta^9; the singlet has one channel: sigma = W^2. Each
                   proton carries sqrt(4 pi) W onto the unit static answer, so V/(hbar c) = -4 pi W^2/(4 pi r) =
                   -W^2/r.
  classical form:  Newton, V(r) = -G m_p^2/r; the field term (R - 2 Lambda)/16 pi G, 1/16 pi G = m_p^2/(16 pi W^2 hbar
                   c).
    the law's static answer between the two held sources (F4): the number in front of 1/(4 pi r) is 0.9989, 0.9957, 0.9930, 0.9999 in four directions
    so -r V(r)/(hbar c) = W^2 x (the number above): the coefficient of -1/r is W^2 = 5.906152e-39
  what remains:
    D04   G m_p^2/(hbar c) x 1e39                5.90615249377          measured 5.90614943 +0.000133/-0.000133  +0.02 standard deviations
    D05   M_Pl x 1e-19 [GeV]                     1.22088981189          measured 1.22089 +1.4e-05/-1.4e-05  -0.01 standard deviations

EXPERIMENT A2. Light and a gyroscope passing a held mass
  held:            a light ray grazing a held mass; a gyroscope carried around it on a free orbit.
  the law returns: the light's direction carried around the frame's curvature, against Newton's half: the frame term's
                   field equation, with the number of A1 in front, gives 1 + gamma = 2; the frame carried around the
                   closed orbit, against the flat frame, gives Einstein's geodetic drift, ratio 1; at second order the
                   bending carries 15 pi/4.
  classical form:  the deflection 2(1 + gamma) GM/(b c^2) + (15 pi/4)(GM/b c^2)^2; the geodetic drift over its
                   Einstein value.
  what remains:
    H01   1 + gamma                              2                      measured 2.000021 +2.3e-05/-2.3e-05  -0.91 standard deviations
    H02   geodetic drift / Einstein              1                      measured 0.99934908645 +0.00277/-0.00277  +0.23 standard deviations
    L18   second-order bending 15 pi/4           11.780972451           prediction

EXPERIMENT A3. Two clocks at two heights compare the fine structure; bodies of every composition fall together
  held:            two atomic clocks held at different gravitational potentials, comparing alpha; bodies of different
                   make in one field.
  the law returns: alpha is a coefficient of the law, the count at the plane hk (C_h/M)(e^2/N_2)/(1 - x), the same at
                   every location: the stationary weight on the singlet does not enter it. A world line's
                   gravitational charge is its self-interaction at the singlet, where its interaction with itself and
                   its interaction with another are one number: its mass. The potential is a lapse N on the clock that
                   measures energy; a world line's rest pole sits where its kernel vanishes, K_X(E, N) = K_X(E/N, 1),
                   so K_N = -(E/N) K_E and dE_X/dN = E_X(N)/N; at N = 1, dE_X/dN = E_X(1): the lapse couples to the
                   rest energy the world line's own clock measures, the same share for every world line.
  classical form:  d log alpha/d(Phi/c^2) = 0; universality of free fall, (dE_X/dN)/E_X = 1/N for every X, equal to 1
                   at N = 1.
  what remains:
    D07   d log alpha/d(Phi/c^2)                 0                      measured 14 +11/-11  -1.27 standard deviations

EXPERIMENT A4. The frame held curved: the constant term
  held:            the ten rotations split at h into six that keep it and four that move it, e/l; l varied (F7).
  the law returns: the curvature of the ten rotations, F = R - e^e/l^2, contracted with h in the epsilon contraction:
                   -(4/l^2)(R - 6/l^2) vol, at every l and curvature.
  classical form:  Einstein-Cartan with Lambda: R - 2 Lambda, Lambda l^2 = 3; the constant term's pressure is minus
                   its density.
    Lambda l^2 = 3.000000000000, 3.000000000000, 3.000000000000, 3.000000000000 at l = 0.5, 1, 1.7, 3 (F7)
  what remains:
    L08   w of the constant term                 -1                     prediction

EXPERIMENT A5. The whole system at rest: the constant term in the unit of the step
  held:            the whole system at rest; the angle the electron's clock turns during 1/(E l) of a proton Compton
                   period, tau = 2 pi/(E l m_p/m_e); one arrival at a symmetric state s = e/N_2 = 3/50.
  the law returns: 3 W^6 tau s^3: the frame's constant term measured in the step, the singlet's transmission factor W
                   six times.
  classical form:  Lambda l_P^2 = 3 Omega_Lambda H_0^2 l_P^2/c^2; the de Sitter radius l, its temperature k_B T = hbar
                   c/(2 pi l), its entropy 3 pi/(Lambda l_P^2).
  what remains:
    D06   Lambda l_P^2 x 1e122                   2.85522324301          measured 2.8451 +0.076/-0.076  +0.13 standard deviations
    T03   de Sitter radius l [Mpc]               5369.08213305          de Sitter convention
    T04   de Sitter k_B T [eV]                   1.89564063246e-34      de Sitter convention
    L10   de Sitter entropy 3 pi/Lambda l_P^2    3.30089003858e+122     identity with D06

B. ELECTROMAGNETISM: the plane hk, type 2|4, u = -1/4, its central rotation the common clock

EXPERIMENT B1. Coulomb: two unit charges held at rest at a distance r
  held:            two sources of unit charge on the central rotation of the plane hk, at rest, at distances r from 4
                   to 18 steps.
  the law returns: the law answers a gauge field on the links only through its curvature around the squares, which no
                   gauge transformation changes (F5); a term without the curvature would change under a gauge
                   transformation, so the rotation carries no mass and its static answer is 1/(4 pi r) (F4). In front
                   of 1/r stands what the two sources bring to the plane hk: each brings its reflection leaving the
                   plane, e = k2/k0 = 3/5, on the transitions that keep its charge, the C_h/M = 60/296 along h, over
                   the N_2 = 10 channels of the symmetric states, the clock's contact x closed once: sigma =
                   (C_h/M)(e^2/N_2)/(1 - x) = alpha; each source carries sqrt(4 pi) onto the unit static answer, so
                   V/(hbar c) = 4 pi alpha/(4 pi r) = alpha/r.
  classical form:  Coulomb, V(r) = alpha hbar c/r; the field term -F^2/(16 pi alpha).
    the law's static answer between the two held sources (F4): the number in front of 1/(4 pi r) is 0.9989, 0.9957, 0.9930, 0.9999 in four directions
    so r V(r)/(hbar c) = alpha x (the number above): the coefficient of 1/r is 1/137.035999177
  what remains:
    D02   1/alpha                                137.035999177          measured 137.035999177 +2.1e-08/-2.1e-08  +0.00 standard deviations
    L19   1/alpha at h = 1                       137.035999147          bound for every clock

EXPERIMENT B2. The field turned on: the field's own term
  held:            phases theta on the forty links at amplitudes 0.1, 0.03, 0.01, and a pure gauge transformation
                   (F5).
  the law returns: log det(I - wA_-[e^(i theta)]) - log det(I - wA_-) = -(kappa/2)|C theta|^2, kappa = 1/200 at the
                   plane hk; a gauge transformation returns nothing. The field in units of the charge is the link
                   phase per cell in units of the phase a unit charge carries: int F^2 = 8 pi kappa alpha |C theta|^2
                   = 9.1701e-04 |C theta|^2.
  classical form:  Maxwell, D_mu F^mu nu = 4 pi alpha j^nu, d F = 0; a held electric fact has no drift of its own:
                   alpha is the same at every location and phase.
    kappa at amplitude 0.01: 0.00499972 (1/200 = 0.005)
  what remains:
    L09   drift of an electric fact              0                      prediction

EXPERIMENT B3. Nucleons held in a magnetic field
  held:            a proton, a neutron and a deuteron at rest in a held field B; the precession frequency grows in
                   proportion to B.
  the law returns: the proton's moment is the spread of its excursion's length, Var l = 156, over the 2N_2 channels of
                   the symmetric states, less the plane's own coupling once, eps2 = alpha^2/(1 + alpha/N_2), over E
                   l^2 b: mu_p = [Var l/(2N_2)(1 - eps2/(E l^2 b))]^(1/2); the neutron's is -4(1 + E n_F)/23 with the
                   same factor; the deuteron's comes from the two, its binding and the neutron's share.
  classical form:  Larmor, hbar w = 2 mu B, mu in nuclear magnetons.
  what remains:
    G03   mu_p                                   2.7928473453           measured 2.79284734463 +8.2e-10/-8.2e-10  +0.81 standard deviations
    G04   mu_n                                   -1.91304302381         measured -1.91304276 +4.5e-07/-4.5e-07  -0.59 standard deviations
    G05   mu_n/mu_p                              -0.684979444733        measured -0.68497935 +1.6e-07/-1.6e-07  -0.59 standard deviations
    G13   mu_d                                   0.857438233519         measured 0.8574382335 +2.2e-09/-2.2e-09  +0.01 standard deviations

EXPERIMENT B4. Electrons scattered off a proton and a pion at small momentum transfer
  held:            the momentum transfer q held small and varied; the slope of the electric form factor.
  the law returns: the proton's charge is spread over four steps, r_p = 4 lambda_p; the pion's over the visits of one
                   excursion to the symmetric states, r_pi = (E n_F)^(1/2) lambda_p.
  classical form:  G_E(q^2) = 1 - q^2 <r^2>/6.
  what remains:
    G01   r_p [fm]                               0.841235640213         measured 0.84075 +0.00064/-0.00064  +0.76 standard deviations
    S04   pion charge radius [fm]                0.665055167996         measured 0.659 +0.004/-0.004  +1.51 standard deviations

EXPERIMENT B5. The classical theory carries alpha and the rest clocks: the precision experiments of electrodynamics
  held:            an electron in a Penning trap, the hydrogen series, alpha carried to the Z pole, the muon's
                   anomaly.
  the law returns: the law's long-wave motion, quantum electrodynamics, carries the computed alpha, the rest clocks
                   and the computed vector current to each measurement and brings no number of its own.
