C. THE REST CLOCKS: the own clock i g_h, kept on the plane {n, h} as the world line's time, moved at the divided set {h}, where its rate is the mass

EXPERIMENT C1. The electron: one transition held at rest
  held:            a world line at rest, its clock turning by a phase theta per step on one of the 320 transitions;
                   theta varied (F9).
  the law returns: exactly, D_theta(u) = D(u) + (e^(-i theta) - 1) u D'(u)/320: every transition has the same
                   cofactor, so the law's zero turns by theta/320 + O(theta^3) per step, with d arg(4u_c)/d theta =
                   1/320 at theta = 0, the unit rate.
  classical form:  E = hbar w = m c^2: the electron is the unit.
    turn per step x 320 at theta = 1e-4: 0.999999998

EXPERIMENT C2. The proton beside the electron: two clocks compared
  held:            the proton and the electron's marked transition held at rest side by side, their clocks compared as
                   a trap compares two cyclotron frequencies (F9).
  the law returns: each of the proton's M = 296 available transitions compares the moment with itself, <Omega, (L +
                   g_h x g_s) Omega> = 6 + [s = h]: the comparison's value at the singlet on every transition and one
                   more on the C_h = 60 transitions along its own time; so the zero turns 6M + C_h = 1836 times as
                   fast as for the electron; then the Gram-determinant term, the singlet's grade factor k0(-1/4) =
                   5/2, the inverse of the transmission, per unit of L(Omega); less the signed-volume terms, a^5 on
                   the five vector states and b a^6 with b = 7/16: L(Omega) M + C_h + log k0(-1/4)/L(Omega) - a^5 - b
                   a^6.
  classical form:  E = m c^2 for both, their ratio; the step is the proton's reduced Compton length, lambda_p =
                   0.2103089101 fm.
    the clocks' ratio from the law's zero at theta -> 0: 1836.000000; with the Gram-determinant and signed-volume terms: 1836.152673412
  what remains:
    J01   m_p/m_e                                1836.15267341          measured 1836.152673426 +3.2e-08 / −3.2e-08  -0.44 standard deviations
    B12   m_p/m_e                                1836.15267341          measured 1836.152673426 +3.2e-08/-3.2e-08  -0.44 standard deviations
    M1    m_p [MeV]                              938.27208942           measured 938.27208943 ± 2.9e-07  -0.03 standard deviations

